course: dictionary
lesson: 3078
title: Edited, not always real
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Edited means someone checked and changed a piece of writing, a photo or a film to make it better. Writers edit their stories by fixing spelling and punctuation, and by swapping in better words.
explain: Edited is the past form of edit. It can be a verb, as in «someone edited the photo», or an adjective that describes a text, photo or video that has been changed from the original.
explain: Context helps. «Edited and fake photos often spread after big events» tells you that some pictures have been changed, and some are not real at all. Edited does not always mean fake, but an edited picture is no longer the original.
explain: Check the clues. If a photo seems too perfect, too shocking or too strange, pause before you share it. An adult can help you do a reverse image search, which shows where else the picture appears and whether it is the original.
fact: Edit means to check and change something to make it better.
fact: Edited is the past form of edit, so it describes something that has already been changed.
fact: An edited text, photo or video has been changed from the original.
fact: «Edited» can also be an adjective, as in «an edited version» or «a heavily edited film».
fact: Not everything online is real, because photos and videos can be edited, and some are fake.
exercise: «Edited and fake photos often spread after big events.» What does edited mean here? | Taken by a camera with no changes | Printed on paper | *Checked and changed from the original | Deleted forever
exercise: Find one word in «Edited and fake photos often spread after big events» that warns a photo might not be real. | spread | events | *fake | photos
exercise: A film is described as «heavily edited». What does this suggest? | It is made of paper | *It has been changed a lot from the original | It is very quiet | It was filmed in one take with no changes
test: Which word is the past form of edit? | *edited | editing | edits | editor
test: An edited photo is one that has | stayed exactly the same as the original | been printed on paper | *been changed from the original | been deleted
exam: Your friend shares a photo that looks unreal. What should you do first? | Believe it because it is online | Edit it yourself and then share it | Share it quickly before it disappears | *Ask whether it may be edited, and check with an adult using a reverse image search
